<% content_for :title, "Connect via SMART on FHIR - Medride" %>

<h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6">Connect via SMART on FHIR</h1>

<section class="mb-10">
  <h2 class="text-lg font-medium mb-2">Via the SMART Health IT launcher (recommended)</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-2">
    Works for both launch types — the launcher's "EHR Launch" mode redirects
    here with <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 rounded px-1">iss</code> +
    <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 rounded px-1">launch</code> set; its
    "Standalone Launch" mode redirects here with just <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 rounded px-1">iss</code>,
    and <%= link_to "smart/launch", smart_ehr_launch_url %> detects which one it got and
    requests the right scope either way. Make sure you're signed in as a
    coordinator in this browser first, then:
  </p>
  <ol class="text-sm text-gray-500 list-decimal list-inside space-y-1">
    <li>Go to <a href="https://launch.smarthealthit.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="underline">launch.smarthealthit.org</a></li>
    <li>Set "App Launch URL" to <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 rounded px-1"><%= smart_ehr_launch_url %></code></li>
    <li>Pick either launch type, configure a simulated patient, and click Launch</li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="text-lg font-medium mb-2">Bring your own iss</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    Initiates login ourselves against any FHIR server's SMART endpoints, no
    launcher round-trip needed — the authorization server prompts for a
    patient during login. Note: launch.smarthealthit.org's bare
    <code class="font-mono text-xs bg-gray-100 rounded px-1">/v/r4/fhir</code>
    endpoint rejects this (its authorize endpoint expects launch context
    minted via their launcher UI, even for "standalone") — this box is for a
    real EHR sandbox's SMART-enabled iss that supports launching without
    that round-trip.
  </p>

  <%= form_with url: smart_launch_path, method: :post, class: "flex gap-2" do |f| %>
    <%= f.text_field :iss, class: "border rounded px-3 py-2 flex-1 font-mono text-sm",
          placeholder: "FHIR server base URL (iss)" %>
    <%= f.submit "Connect via SMART on FHIR", class: "bg-gray-900 text-white rounded px-4 py-2 cursor-pointer whitespace-nowrap" %>
  <% end %>
</section>
